isited first, and once they are [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]exhausted `Tab` resumes the enclosing snippet at the stop after the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]one that was nested into. Tabstop anchors survive arbitrary editing[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]because they are remapped from real document deltas, `Shift+Tab` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]steps backwards through the visited stops, and the whole session [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]state machine lives in the Rust core so any future frontend gets [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the same behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]nested_snippet_sessions.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/nested_snippet_sessions.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-kz[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-kz/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust snippet expansion planner[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_expansion[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_expansion: add a pure Rust expansion planner that turns a template [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plus its insertion context into cleaned text and ordered tabstop [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]offsets, and make it the single owner of unescaped-tabstop scanning.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust nested snippet session state machine[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_session[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_expansion[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_session: add the pure session state machine over a flat ordered [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stop list — nest-vs-reset on expand, advance/retreat, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]absolute-anchor remapping from document edit deltas.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]PyO3 binding and wire parity for the session engine[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_binding[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_session[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_binding: expose the session state machine to Python as a single [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire-shaped binding, with binding-level tests and the lib.rs binding [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inventory updated.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python facade for the snippet session engine[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]py_facade[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_binding[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py_facade: add a validated Python facade over the new binding, register [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the binding name with the core validator, and prove the round trip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against a locally built core.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rewrite the prompt widget snippet mixin over the session [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]engine[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]widget_engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py_facade[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]widget_engine: replace the from-doc-end tabstop queue with the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]facade-backed session, feed every document mutation through a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]TextArea.edit hook, and swap the raw _snippet_tabstops reads for a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]session-active predicate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Nest-vs-reset policy for every non-trigger expansion caller[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]call_sites[dim] · [dim][/dim]after widget_engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]call_sites: make each of the five non-trigger callers of the expansion [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]entry point declare whether it nests inside the active session or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]replaces it, and cover the whole-pane skeleton reset.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shift+Tab backward tabstop navigation[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]back_nav[dim] · [dim][/dim]after widget_engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]back_nav: turn the consumed Shift+Tab no-op into a retreat through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already-visited stops, across nesting boundaries, without disturbing the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bullet and ordered-list dedent path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation and core version pin[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs_pin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after call_sites, back_nav[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs_pin: document nested sessions and backward navigation in the ACE [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and editor guides, update the keymap tables and CHANGELOG, and raise the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core-rs floor once the core release lands.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-kz","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-kz.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-a99e458c3612bb36ddb5ed3c41e66a94","started_at":"2026-08-13T16:33:52.507980+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"64720434d88ceca1afe5412289f9ccc183798d6ad30010b2ec0adc6aa13aa391","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-kz.5/commits.json","size_